// SR 748.941 — Chapter 1 Scope of Application and Common Provisions
// generated by src/parse.py. Do not edit by hand.

:NOTE
English is not an official language of the Swiss Confederation. This translation is provided for information purposes only and has no legal force.

:INFO
Art. 1 Scope of application
This Ordinance applies to:
a. manned special category aircraft: hang gliders, both unpowered and with an electric motor, kites, paragliders, tethered balloons and parachutes;
b. unmanned aircraft: kites, paragliders, tethered balloons, free-flying balloons, model aircraft and other unmanned aircraft.
|

:INFO
Art. 2 Aircraft register and airworthiness
1 Aircraft under Article 1 are not entered in the aircraft register.
2 Their airworthiness is not tested.
3 No noise certificates are issued.
|

:INFO
Art. 3 Place of take-off and landing
1 Aircraft under Article 1 are not required to take off from or land at an aerodrome.
2 The exemption under paragraph 1 does not apply to hang gliders with an electric motor.
3 The rights of landowners to prevent trespassing and to compensation for any damage apply in all cases.
|

:INFO
Art. 4 Public air shows
No authorisation is required from the Federal Office of Civil Aviation (FOCA) for public air shows that exclusively involve the use of aircraft under Article 1.
|

:INFO
Art. 5 Commercial flights
No authorisation is required from the FOCA for commercial flights using aircraft under Article 1.
|

:INFO
Art. 6 References to SERA
The provisions of the Annex to Implementing Regulation (EU) No 923/2012 are referred to with the abbreviation «SERA» and the relevant number.
|

:NOTE
SERA = Standardised European Rules of the Air.

